          "source_text_sha256": "46bcd471e4523c5d1052aad206eb16ed48d80d965f7ccdef37d3f7bcb304e74e",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On July 20, 2015, two people at their home were intrigued by the slow movement in the sky of an object with several lights of different colors. A rumbling engine sound was heard. The PAN moved straight from North to South. The observation lasted between 4 and 7 minutes. Only one testimony was reported to GEIPAN. Given the elements collected (see the investigation report), namely:\n\n- Observation of lights with colors identical to those of aircraft navigation lights.\n- Correct positioning of these lights in relation to the direction of movement of PAN and the position of the witnesses.\n- Observation of a searchlight beam comparable to that equipped on civil security and gendarmerie helicopters.\n- Perception of a motor noise identical to that of an airplane.\n\nGEIPAN classified this case as \"B\" as a probable observation of a helicopter. Due to the low strangeness of the observation, GEIPAN did not conduct inquiries with the national gendarmerie or air traffic control.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "6ca6b24fe11778c965ce61e166f0886c7d1c1ff53a5f1aeed9ac0d4ec309253b"
        }
